  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# Barrier feedback (owner: Miguel)\n\nStores the web app's \"Já não está\" answers so the team can review them per barrier at the end of the day.\nAn answer never removes a barrier.\n\n- **In:** `access/barriers/<barrier id>/feedback`, not retained, `{id, barrier_id, answer: \"gone\", answered_at, lat?, lon?}`.\n- **Out (all retained, QoS 1):**\n  - `access/feedback/<barrier id>/answers/<feedback id>`: the answer, unchanged;\n  - `access/feedback/<barrier id>/gone_count`: number of distinct answers;\n  - `access/feedback/<barrier id>/last_answered_at`: `answered_at` of the latest one.\n\nAn answer whose `id` was already stored is ignored, so the app's outbox resends and QoS 1 duplicates count once.\nOnly `answer: \"gone\"` with an `id` of letters, digits, `_` or `-` (at most 64) is stored; the id becomes a topic level.\nThe barrier id comes from the topic, never from the payload.\n\nOn broker 2.22.0 `PUBLISH MODEL` ignored the model's `RETAIN` and dropped a `WITH TIMESTAMP` field, so the summary\nis plain retained topics. The count is read back from its own retained topic. Broker durability is on, so the answers\nand counts survive a restart (verified 24/10).\n\nReview: `explore_topics` with filter `access/feedback/`, or subscribe to `access/feedback/+/gone_count`.\n\n**Two stores, on purpose (decided 24/10).**\n- **Supabase** (Ben's `BarriersDB` in `10-barriers-db.lotnb`, table `barrier_feedback`, view `barrier_review`) is the\n  long-term record and the end-of-day review for **app reports** (ids `b…`). `schema.sql` rejects every other id.\n- **This broker store** gives live counts over MQTT (the operator panel reads `gone_count`) and is the **only** record\n  for answers about `city-*` and `demo-*` barriers. It needs no database, so it also works when Supabase is not\n  connected (today the broker has no `SUPABASE_*` env/secret, so `BarriersDB` is not loaded)."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION StoreBarrierFeedback\nON TOPIC \"access/barriers/+/feedback\" DO\n    SET \"barrier_id\" WITH TOPIC POSITION 3\n    SET \"feedback_id\" WITH GET JSON \"id\" IN PAYLOAD AS STRING\n    SET \"answer\" WITH GET JSON \"answer\" IN PAYLOAD AS STRING\n    SET \"answered_at\" WITH GET JSON \"answered_at\" IN PAYLOAD AS STRING\n    IF {answer} == \"gone\" AND {feedback_id} MATCHES REGEX \"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}$\" THEN\n        SET \"base\" WITH \"access/feedback/\" + {barrier_id}\n        SET \"answer_topic\" WITH {base} + \"/answers/\" + {feedback_id}\n        SET \"seen\" WITH GET TOPIC {answer_topic} AS STRING\n        IF {seen} == \"\" THEN\n            PUBLISH TOPIC {answer_topic} WITH PAYLOAD WITH RETAIN QOS1\n            SET \"count\" WITH GET TOPIC {base} + \"/gone_count\" AS INT\n            PUBLISH TOPIC {base} + \"/gone_count\" WITH {count} + 1 WITH RETAIN QOS1\n            PUBLISH TOPIC {base} + \"/last_answered_at\" WITH {answered_at} WITH RETAIN QOS1"
  }
]
